   124	## Exact native signatures and Python stub
   125	
   126	Declarations are the required signatures, not skeleton implementation bodies. Locally permit too_many_arguments as Isaiah does. Every ndarray borrow lasts the whole operation. Error mapping: admission/grammar/engine → PyValueError with env/seat/field; seed range/arithmetic → PyOverflowError; caught panic → PyRuntimeError. No partial result. Exact keyword-only signatures:
   127	
   128	```rust
   129	#[pyclass(name = "KaggricultureEnv", module = "owl.rs")]
   130	pub struct PyKaggricultureEnv { /* owned pool, games, staging, records, seeds */ }
   131	
   132	#[pymethods]
   133	impl PyKaggricultureEnv {
   134	    #[new]
   135	    #[pyo3(signature = (n_envs, seed, seed_stride, config, reward_config, native_threads, *, hire_limit))]
   136	    fn new(py: Python<'_>, n_envs: usize,
   137	        seed: &Bound<'_, PyAny>, seed_stride: &Bound<'_, PyAny>,
   138	        config: &str, reward_config: &Bound<'_, PyDict>,
